      "content": "thanks. obsidian sounds good. i want to make sure nothing gets corrupted during the transfer from my mind to the system. i'll start with a high-priority entry from my childhood—a very specific sequence of sounds and colors from a park i visited in 1998. i need to be extremely precise with the timestamps and the sensory metadata so the integrity of the archive is maintained. can you help me design a template for these entries? i need fields for things like 'atmospheric pressure', 'ambient noise frequency', and 'visual saturation levels' so the data is perfect.",
